# <Name> Lightroom Preset — Characteristics

**Category**: Decade

<2-4 sentence overview that names the preset and contains the phrase "Lightroom preset".>

## Historical Context
## Photographic Technology
(film/plate stock, process, chemistry, format, camera, printing — whatever applies)
## Visual Signature
(colour palette with concrete hue/behaviour claims, contrast structure, grain/texture, tonal distribution)
## Tonal Register
**Register**: <one of: cool-overcast | neutral | warm-golden | high-key | low-key | sepia-toned | ...>
<2-4 sentences justifying it, and how the preset should behave against it. This section is MANDATORY — the repo requires each preset's intended tonal register to be recorded and validated against.>
## Lighting & Subject Matter
## Lightroom Translation
Panel-by-panel mapping of how the preset implements the look, citing the ACTUAL values from the XMP (Basic panel, Tone Curve, Color Grading, HSL, Grain, Effects).
## Verification
Does the XMP match the register and the defining traits? State pass/adjustments.
## Sources
- [Title](https://real-url) — what it contributed
(at least 3, real and checkable)
## See Also
- [Decade presets](../../docs/decade.md)
- links to 2-3 genuinely related presets in this repo, e.g. `../Victorian-Daguerreotype/` style folder links
```

